      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're getting the hang of it. Yes, if you use the chair for 90% of the time for work, you can claim 90% of the cost as a business expense. It's like a cleverly hidden compartment in your chair, where you can stash the tax savings. \n\nNow, about those software subscriptions and office snacks. You're right to wonder if you need to track them individually or group them under \"office supplies.\" Think of it like a stash of gold coins in a goblin's lair - you want to keep track of each one, but also keep an eye on the overall hoard. \n\nFor the software subscriptions, you can group them under \"Software\" or \"Professional Fees\" in QuickBooks. This way, you can track the individual subscriptions and their costs, and also see the overall impact on your business expenses. \n\nAs for the office snacks, you can group them under \"Office Supplies\" or \"Miscellaneous\" in QuickBooks. However, be sure to keep a record of which snacks you bought for which clients, as this can help you track the business use percentage for those expenses. After all, a goblin's love for snacks can be a double-edged sword - it can",
